      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Peer Review: Quantum Coherence in Disordered Topological Insulators at Room Temperature\n\n# Methodology and Sample Preparation\nThe chemical vapor deposition and rapid thermal annealing protocols lack sufficient detail regarding substrate uniformity and dopant distribution, which are critical for interpreting coherence times in disordered systems.\n\n# Microwave Measurement and Noise Floor\nThe reported 3:1 signal-to-noise ratio in pulsed EPR spectroscopy appears insufficient to rule out environmental noise artifacts that could artificially inflate coherence measurements.\n\n# Conclusion\nA revised manuscript is required to address these methodological gaps and provide rigorous validation of the noise floor before publication.",
